The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a series of dot plots, and Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, demonstrate that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone shows limited uptake, complexing OVA with Nano-11 dramatically increases the amount of OVA internalized by BMDCs. This finding, assessed by flow cytometry, highlights Nano-11's role as an effective delivery vehicle, enhancing antigen presentation to critical immune cells.